}

NOTES: Use an OrthographicCamera in a standard isometric pose for the axonometric look. Render the three planes as PlaneGeometry meshes with MeshBasicMaterial (transparent, depthWrite:false, side:DoubleSide) and sort them into a single render group so overlap tints blend evenly; add LineSegments outlines from EdgesGeometry for the sheet borders. Axes: solid Line + LineDashedMaterial (call computeLineDistances) for the occluded stretches, plus Mesh cones for arrowheads. All text via canvas-texture Sprites so it stays upright and readable while orbiting; keep sprite scale constant in world units. Octant hover uses invisible Box meshes (visible:false is not raycastable, so use material.opacity 0 with transparent:true) intersected by Raycaster; on hover, fade in a thin colored box and swap the label sprite texture to a larger variant. The plane-emphasis toggle raises the chosen sheet's opacity to ~0.8, drops the other two to ~0.15, and tints the two half-spaces with large faint boxes (e.g. warm for the positive side, cool for the negative side) plus a small legend reading 'z > 0 / z < 0'. OrbitControls with damping, no pan, limited zoom; a 'reset view' snap back to the source pose.

